# Kitchen timers: `timer` starts one, `timers` lists them, `timer off`
# cancels; when the time is up a window opens with the message.
@ai
$ ai control on
$ timers
no timers ('timer 10m tea' starts one)
$ timer 1h bake bread
timer 1: 1h 00m (a window and a tune when it is up)
$ timer 2s tea is ready
timer 2: 2s (a window and a tune when it is up)
$ timers
~ ^  2 +[12]s left  tea is ready$
~ ^  1 +(1h 00m|59m \d\ds) left  bake bread$
$ timer off 1
timer 1 cancelled
$ timer off 1
timer: no timer 1 ('timers' lists them)
$ sleep 3
@ctl text {machine}
~ ^--- window \d+: Timer 2 ---$
~ Time is up: tea is ready
$ timers
no timers ('timer 10m tea' starts one)
$ timer soon
usage: timer DURATION [MESSAGE]   (90, 90s, 5m, 1h30m; up to a day) | timer off N
# alarm: at the next time the local clock shows (QEMU's clock is set from the host).
$ alarm 25:00
usage: alarm HH:MM [MESSAGE]   (the next time the local clock shows it)
$ alarm 03:15 milk the bees
~ ^alarm \(timer 3\) at 03:15: in (\d+h \d\dm|\d+m \d\ds|\d+s) \('timer off 3' cancels\)$
$ timers
~ ^  3 +\S.* left  milk the bees$
$ timer off 3
timer 3 cancelled
